Thanks Ira for the tip about the change to the tree structure for the pwg 
site. That was my problem.

I placed the slides that we worked on during today's FSG Arch meeting on 
the pwg site at:
ftp://ftp.pwg.org/pub/pwg/fsg/April2006-OSDL-Printing-Summit-Slides/2006-03-15-FSG_Overview_OSDL_Printing_Summit_Draft.ppt

I extracted the JT slides from the original PWG-Apple slides from 
2005-07-14 and put them on the PWG site at:
ftp://ftp.pwg.org/pub/pwg/fsg/April2006-OSDL-Printing-Summit-Slides/2006-03-15-FSG_JTAPI_OSDL_Printing_Summit_Draft.ppt
There are currently 15 slides that we can cut down in the next FSG Arch 
meeting.

I extracted the PAPI slides from the original PWG-Apple slides from 
2005-07-14 and put them on the PWG site at:
ftp://ftp.pwg.org/pub/pwg/fsg/April2006-OSDL-Printing-Summit-Slides/2006-03-15-FSG_PAPI_OSDL_Printing_Summit_Draft.ppt
There are currently 7 slides, so Norm may be able to use this presentation 
as is.

Claudia

